<title>NORWAY: KVAERNER RAISES STAKE IN VYBORG SHIPYARD.</title>
<headline>KVAERNER RAISES STAKE IN VYBORG SHIPYARD.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipbuilding, engineering and construction group Kvaerner ASA said on Wednesday it had increased its stake in JSC Vyborg Shipyard in Russia to 75 percent from 42 percent of voting shares.</p>
<p>Kvaerner said its investment to date in the yard totalled 50 million crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;Kvaerner will primarily use the shipyard in its development strategy for the offshore industry and in the construction of various specialty ships,&quot; the company said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
